  "_why_f04_6_r29": "Environment grade (haze #9cb7d3 at 0.001, contrast 1.1, saturation 1.08) and the warm 38-degree sun: ON (CPU-provisional improvement, not a closure): F04#6 r29 mapped 6.38 Bar A vs shipping 5.91 with three code-blind judges on the fixed F04-6 camera set (Low/Compatibility, llvmpipe; ralph/reports/LOOK/close-1022/F04-6.md). Parked by the gain rule; a GPU pass decides, and a GPU score below the bar reopens it.",
  "light_candidate": {"_why": "Group 3 (vis-meadows, 1 Nov, OFF until GPU-judged): the batch-1 judges' ask common to every Meadows stand, 'flat midday light and crushed night frames; a warm key light with rim, aerial fog, and night fill so subjects read'. meadows_look.gd::light_candidate_look merges `look` over art.json + this file for the Meadows rig only. Day: the key sun turns warmer and a little lower (-38 -> -33 deg, 1.5 -> 1.65, #ffe8c4 -> #ffdfb4) for longer modelling shadows; characters get a soft rim (player_character_rim_scale 0 -> 0.35); aerial fog roughly doubles (0.001 -> 0.0019, fog_sky_affect 0 -> 0.3, aerial_perspective 0.7 -> 0.9) so the distance layers into blue haze. Night: more fill so bodies read (ambient 1.5 -> 1.95, exposure 1.2 -> 1.35, moon 0.55 -> 0.72, shadow opacity 0.68 -> 0.58), and a tighter moon glow (sun_glow 0.15 -> 0.07, falloff 55 -> 95) for the banded halo the P2-003 judges named. Golden keeps its own block. Presentation only.", "enabled": true, "look": {"sun": {"pitch_deg": -33.0, "energy": 1.65, "colour": "#ffdfb4"}, "environment": {"fog_density": 0.0019, "fog_sky_affect": 0.3, "aerial_perspective": 0.9, "player_character_rim_scale": 0.35}, "times": {"night": {"sun": {"energy": 0.72, "shadow_opacity": 0.58}, "sky": {"sun_glow": 0.07, "sun_glow_falloff": 95.0}, "environment": {"ambient_energy": 1.95, "exposure": 1.35}}}}}
